name    top
prog    top -a 3
# The process lister.  It refreshes for ever, so the test is: does it draw
# its table with this session's own two processes in it, and does it still
# do so after a refresh?  Until 2026-09-18 it printed the headings and took
# a bus error -- see SRC/eff_top/README.OSK -- so `bash' appearing here is
# the whole point of the case.
rate    0.6
wait    8
snap    listed
expect  Id PId Grp.Usr Prio
expect  bash
expect  top
# WITHOUT THESE THE CASE CANNOT FAIL.  The crash dump top used to produce
# carries the headings, `bash' and `top' in it too -- measured 2026-09-18,
# the old binary PASSED the three `expect' lines above.  What tells the two
# apart is the dump itself.
absent  Process Aborted
absent  E_PRCABT
absent  Last syscall
wait    8
snap    refreshed
key     \003
wait    2
